      <Abstract>
         <Short WordCount="79">
            <AbsText HTMLContent="true">&lt;html&gt;            &lt;head&gt;              &lt;meta name="ValidationSchema" content="http://www.w3.org/2002/08/xhtml/xhtml1-strict.xsd"/&gt;              &lt;title/&gt;            &lt;/head&gt;            &lt;body&gt;              &lt;p&gt;   Many D.C. properties are subject to the city's rent control law, which regulates how much rent landlords can charge and when they can raise rents. If you live in a rent-controlled building, landlords can raise the rent once every 180 days, or twice a year, but only if the Housing Regulation Administration grants the owners a rent- ceiling increase. To find out if you live in a building that's covered, call the Housing Regulation Administration at 202-442- 4600.&lt;/p&gt;            &lt;/body&gt;          &lt;/html&gt;</AbsText>
         </Short>
      </Abstract>
